<p>Connect your Paybill or Till number in <strong>Settings › M-Pesa › Add Paybill or Till</strong> with the Daraja API keys (consumer key, secret and passkey) from Safaricom's developer portal. Then press <strong>Receive payments</strong> so Safaricom tells HardPoint about money paid in. The keys are stored encrypted.</p>

<h2>Payment prompts</h2>
<p>At the till, choose M-Pesa and enter the customer's phone number. They get a prompt on their phone for the amount, enter their PIN, and the sale completes itself when Safaricom confirms. If it doesn't go through, the till says why.</p>

<h2>Money paid straight to your Paybill or Till</h2>
<p>When a customer pays by Lipa na M-Pesa themselves, the payment appears on the till within seconds. Pick it to pay the sale. Payments whose account number is an order reference or a customer's account number are matched to that order or account automatically.</p>

<h2>Airtel Money</h2>
<p>Connect your Airtel Money merchant account in <strong>Settings › Airtel Money</strong> with the client ID and secret from Airtel's
  developer portal, press <strong>Test connection</strong>, then give Airtel the callback address shown on that page. At the till, choose
  Airtel Money and send a prompt to the customer's phone; the sale completes when they enter their PIN. You can also type the Airtel Money
  transaction ID instead. If the cashier stops waiting and the customer pays anyway, the payment shows on the till under
  <strong>Received on Airtel Money</strong> to use on a sale.</p>

<h2>Reconciliation</h2>
<p><strong>Reports › M-Pesa reconciliation</strong> lists money received but not yet used on a sale, and M-Pesa codes typed at a till that Safaricom never confirmed, so anything that doesn't match stands out.</p>
